# Dependencies — zero runtime deps by design

## Context

`app/package.json` deliberately has NO `dependencies` block; its only
devDependencies are `typescript` and `vitest`. In-house utilities live in
`app/src/lib/text.ts`. A silently added package (a state library, lodash, a
uuid generator) defeats the point of this dependency-free sample.

## Rule

- DO NOT add, upgrade, or remove entries in `app/package.json` without
  explicit approval in chat.
- Before reaching for a package, check what already exists: `app/src/lib/`
  for text utilities, `app/src/selectors.ts` for derived reads,
  `app/src/actions.ts` for action construction. Extend the in-house code
  instead (see custom-lib.mdc).
- If a dependency is truly justified, PROPOSE it in chat first — name, why the
  in-house alternative is insufficient, footprint — and wait for approval.
  NEVER just edit `package.json` or run `npm install <pkg>` on your own.
- NEVER commit `node_modules/` or a lockfile change produced by an unapproved
  install.

## How to verify

1. `git diff app/package.json` → empty, or contains no new `dependencies`/`devDependencies` entries.
2. `app/package.json` still has no `dependencies` block and exactly `typescript` + `vitest` under `devDependencies`.
3. `git status --short` → no `node_modules/` paths staged or committed.
